# ── C# build output ──
bin/
obj/

# The published launcher is copied to the repo root so it runs in place against
# runtime/, versions/ and servers/. It is the self-contained build on purpose:
# only that build can serve updates to the other machines, so hosting from here
# works. Its native WPF DLLs sit beside it and are build output too.
/MinecraftLauncher.dll
/MinecraftLauncher.deps.json
/MinecraftLauncher.runtimeconfig.json
/MinecraftLauncher.pdb
/*_cor3.dll

# ── Claude Code / IDE ──
.claude/
.vs/

# ── Launcher runtime & game files (large / not distributable) ──
runtime/
versions/
servers/
skins/

# ── Regenerated by the game and the launcher ──
# cache/ is compiled chunk-generation classes plus the launcher's Modrinth icon
# cache; config/ is mod settings written the first time the client runs. Both come
# back on their own and differ per machine.
cache/
config/

# ── User state (regenerated) ──
config.txt
computer_uuid.dat
version_manifest_v2.json
*.exe
*.exe.WebView2/
.mixin.out/

# ── Host-only state, created beside the launcher as the host uses it ──
# None of this belongs in the repo, and none of it belongs in the rollout zip
# either — section 8 of HANDOFF.md says why for each one. admin.flag is the whole
# of the gate on the Admin tab, so a copy in the repo would be one `git pull` away
# from handing every machine the required-mods editor and everyone else's crashes.
admin.flag
fleet.json
required-mods.json
required-mods/
crash-inbox/
crash-sent.txt
required-mods-declined.txt
play-blocks.json
play-blocks-cache.json
loader-policy.json
loader-policy-cache.json

# World backups. One zip of the real overworld is ~70 MB.
backups/

# ── Logs / temp ──
**/logs/
**/crash-reports/
*.log
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
launcher_errors.txt
# Written by tools\Why-was-this-blocked.cmd on whichever machine it is run.
antivirus-report.txt
# Written by tools\Test-DownloadHosts.ps1, likewise.
download-hosts-report.txt
# What a filter answered with instead, saved by the same script.
download-hosts-blockpage.txt

# ── Transport copy ──
# tools\Test-DownloadHosts.ps1 is also kept at the repo root, so it can be
# dragged onto a USB stick on its own rather than copying the whole tools\
# folder to a workstation. The copy in tools\ is the source; this one is
# disposable and deliberately untracked. If the two ever drift, the SHA-256 in
# a report's provenance stamp says which of them produced that report.
/Test-DownloadHosts.ps1

# Support bundles written by Collect-Support.cmd, on whichever machine it is run.
Ultimate-MC-support-*/
Ultimate-MC-support-*.zip

# Assembled by tools\Build-WorkstationKit.ps1 for a USB trip. Copies, rebuilt on
# demand; the originals are at the root and in tools\.
Workstation-Kit/
